d girls  were you aware  as an individual of how widespread  women's experiences of sexual  harassment has been uh i was and i have  to say  um uh 10 years ago or so when i was at  city hall as deputy mayor for policing  to the then mayor boris johnson we  published the first ever  violence against women and girls  strategy in a major global city  focusing on specifically many of the  issues  that people are still sadly raising that  are  you know it seems endemic in parts of  our society and that's why for example  uh we brought forward the domestic abuse  bill which is reaching the end of its  passage  uh through the house at the moment uh  which will significantly enhance our  ability to deal  with domestic violence and abuse and why  we're very focused for example  on the problems we're seeing in rape  convictions and have an end-to-end rape  review  which is currently on the blocks should  be published shortly hopefully  that will renew our efforts to try and  achieve justice for those women  who are victimized in that particular  horrendous crime type so there's been a  huge amount going on for some time  i do understand people's frustration  though that we're not making  as fast progress as perhaps they would  have liked but they should be assured  that there is enormous effort going into  this and that's what we'll be outlining  with the prime minister this afternoon  will sexual harassment be looked at as a  specific crime  well this is obviously one of the issues  that we we're asking for views on  at the moment one of the responses to  this terrible crime to sever  everett's terrible killing was for us to  reopen  our call for views um about violence  against women and girls  and we've had something like just in the  last couple of days something like 64  000  uh people have come online at got dot uk  to give us their views about  where they think policy should go into  the future we'll be digesting that over  the weeks to come  and be bringing forward a 