verybody i want to  just ask you a final question about um  astrazeneca and the fact that seven  countries have now suspended  its use um pending at the inquiries  about possible  blood clots as a result of using it um  do you believe that we should now be  looking at the use of of astrazeneca's  because many people have already had  this vaccine  no i don't and the scientists tell us  that  all is well and that the incidence of  these  particular problems is is no greater  than you would expect in the population  at large and that these things naturally  occur anyway  obviously the vaccine's been through  very very stringent testing before it  was  authorized for use we have some of the  highest standards in the world  for medical uh products and for testing  as a former  uh or well in fact founder of the all  party group on life sciences before i  became a minister  i can attest to that um i'm hoping to be  called for a vaccine in the next couple  of weeks myself and if it's astrazeneca  i will happily take it in my arm

